1
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:07,433
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:09,367 --> 00:00:13,100
[hyperventilating]

3
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:14,167
GRAH!

4
00:00:14,167 --> 00:00:16,300
WHY DOES THIS HAVE TO BE REAL?!

5
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:19,967
I said I wanted FIVE MINUTES
without being shot,

6
00:00:19,967 --> 00:00:22,567
but I wasn't thinking so literally!

7
00:00:22,567 --> 00:00:24,400
Beep beep! Okay, break's over!

8
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,467
Your performance review
says you're still not dead,

9
00:00:26,467 --> 00:00:29,367
so time to get shot again!
Gotta get those metrics up!

10
00:00:29,367 --> 00:00:30,767
[whimpering]

11
00:00:30,767 --> 00:00:32,867
I don't want to get shot!

12
00:00:32,867 --> 00:00:37,067
That's what this is really about! Every
dispute is about shooting me or not!

13
00:00:37,067 --> 00:00:40,567
Well, not the aliens. They're more
nuanced because they want to eat me,

14
00:00:40,567 --> 00:00:42,700
but, y'know. Fuck aliens.

15
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:44,767
I mean, is the chopper
going to run out of fuel?

16
00:00:44,767 --> 00:00:45,967
I can't assume that.

17
00:00:45,967 --> 00:00:46,721
What's this?

18
00:00:46,721 --> 00:00:48,800
[mechanical whirring]

19
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,067
[Hunter-Chopper firing]
[mechanical whirring]

20
00:00:50,067 --> 00:00:50,567
Hoh!

21
00:00:51,533 --> 00:00:54,000
Yeah, that's smart. What
don't I make more noise?

22
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,467
Actually, yeah. Get me!

23
00:00:55,467 --> 00:00:57,467
Go get me! I'm in there! Get me!

24
00:00:57,467 --> 00:00:58,867
This isn't going to work...

25
00:00:58,867 --> 00:01:02,067
But all I have to look forward to
is troops storming the place also.

26
00:01:02,067 --> 00:01:04,033
Life's full of blessings like that!

27
00:01:04,033 --> 00:01:06,033
They should put me on a calendar...

28
00:01:06,033 --> 00:01:07,833
And there he is! Okay...!

29
00:01:07,833 --> 00:01:09,000
I have a headstart--

30
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:09,333
Oof!

31
00:01:09,333 --> 00:01:10,833
--of five seconds!

32
00:01:10,833 --> 00:01:11,733
[Hunter-chopper charging]
He's spinning up!

33
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:13,133
[Hunter-Chopper firing]
DIVE! DIVE!

34
00:01:13,133 --> 00:01:14,900
UUUAH! WHIPLASH!

35
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:15,733
BLAH!

36
00:01:15,733 --> 00:01:18,067
YEAH! PUT MY PHOTO ON
A MOTIVATIONAL CALENDAR

37
00:01:18,067 --> 00:01:19,967
THAT SAYS YOUR LIFE COULD BE WORSE!

38
00:01:19,967 --> 00:01:21,533
[Hunter-Chopper firing]
BLAAA-AAA-AAAAH!

39
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:24,433
Holy shit!

40
00:01:25,467 --> 00:01:26,267
YOU MISSED!

41
00:01:28,167 --> 00:01:30,800
BUT YOU WIN AT GOD DOMINOES!

42
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:34,186
SO IS THIS WHAT'S HAPPENING?!
IS REALITY FALLING APART AGAIN?!

43
00:01:34,186 --> 00:01:36,067
[Hunter-Chopper firing]

44
00:01:36,067 --> 00:01:38,733
I FORGOT ME BEING ALIVE IS ENDING THE WORLD!

45
00:01:38,733 --> 00:01:40,867
AND YOU KNOW WHAT? I'M
GOING TO *KEEP* FORGETTING!

46
00:01:40,867 --> 00:01:42,333
OH!

47
00:01:42,333 --> 00:01:42,967
Uh!

48
00:01:42,967 --> 00:01:46,167
YEAH! I WAS DESTINED TO DIE A
LONG TIME AGO, BUT I DIDN'T!

49
00:01:46,167 --> 00:01:47,833
SO NOW THE WORLD'S FALLING APART!

50
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:51,267
THAT SMOKESTACK WENT! NEXT A RIFT
IN THE EARTH IS GOING TO OPEN UP!

51
00:01:51,267 --> 00:01:52,933
AND I'M NOT GOING TO STOP, EITHER!

52
00:01:52,933 --> 00:01:54,667
I'M TAKING ALL OF YOU WITH ME!

53
00:01:54,667 --> 00:01:57,439
IT'S GOING TO GET ALL
LANGOLIERS UP IN THIS BITCH!

54
00:01:58,033 --> 00:01:59,367
[Hunter-chopper alarm]
HOLY FUCK!

55
00:01:59,367 --> 00:02:01,633
HE SHOT THE CHOPPER! THAT'S AWESOME!

56
00:02:01,633 --> 00:02:03,600
AWWWW! SO CLOSE!

57
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:07,033
Yeah! You'd better kill me!
You'd better fucking kill me!

58
00:02:07,033 --> 00:02:09,533
If you don't, your whole
world's going to collapse!

59
00:02:09,533 --> 00:02:11,967
Sucks to be you
and everything you care about!

60
00:02:11,967 --> 00:02:14,133
But seriously, stop shooting me. I hate you.

61
00:02:14,133 --> 00:02:16,000
I might hate everyone--I don't know.

62
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,867
Ohhhhhhh, this is not what I want to see.

63
00:02:18,867 --> 00:02:19,633
Alright...

64
00:02:19,633 --> 00:02:22,233
Okay, I think I bought a little bit of time.

65
00:02:22,233 --> 00:02:25,367
I'm really sure they weren't
expecting me to still be alive now.

66
00:02:25,367 --> 00:02:27,567
I mean, was that tower on purpose?

67
00:02:28,367 --> 00:02:31,600
OH NO! NOT AGAIN!

68
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:32,533
Wait...

69
00:02:32,533 --> 00:02:34,100
Is he circling back?

70
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:36,467
Did he actually NOT see me?

71
00:02:36,467 --> 00:02:39,133
No. No, that's not how my life works.

72
00:02:39,133 --> 00:02:41,633
He left because they're
calling in a missile strike.

73
00:02:41,633 --> 00:02:42,533
MOVE!

74
00:02:43,967 --> 00:02:45,167
This is a problem.

75
00:02:45,167 --> 00:02:46,933
Well, that's a highway up there.

76
00:02:46,933 --> 00:02:48,333
Guess I'm on foot!

77
00:02:48,333 --> 00:02:52,967
God, would it be too much to hope to go
up there and hitchhike my way out of here?

78
00:02:52,967 --> 00:02:54,886
Yeah, probably would.

79
00:02:54,886 --> 00:02:55,661
What's this?

80
00:02:57,233 --> 00:02:58,733
Oh, that did a lot.

81
00:02:58,733 --> 00:03:02,967
Yeah, this is just the work of some crazy
homeless person with access to a junkyard.

82
00:03:02,967 --> 00:03:05,267
It's probably a trap for catching cats.

83
00:03:05,267 --> 00:03:07,833
Actually, for all I know,
this is the rebel base.

84
00:03:07,833 --> 00:03:09,100
...what's left of it.

85
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:13,500
Yeah, let's get out of here and
NOT follow the river for once.

86
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:15,033
Hey, there's nothing up here.

87
00:03:15,033 --> 00:03:18,133
This looks like a hideout for
the Lost Boys from Peter Pan.

88
00:03:18,133 --> 00:03:20,500
I'm pretty sure that
won't keep out the cops!

89
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:23,267
I can't even get to the
road. I'm wasting time here.

90
00:03:23,267 --> 00:03:24,500
I don't know where I need to go,

91
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:28,300
but so far the only correct
answer has been NOT wherever I am.

92
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:30,833
I don't think this is the
base. There would be bodies.

93
00:03:30,833 --> 00:03:34,700
Even if they took them in for interrogation,
they'd kill at least one for kicks.

94
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:38,200
They've gotta get SOMETHING for the
trouble of coming all the way out here.

95
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:40,633
Y'know, this is pretty mucky.

96
00:03:40,633 --> 00:03:44,367
I think it's times like these that
call for a little help from my friends.

97
00:03:44,367 --> 00:03:47,433
Yeah, why don't you talk to them,
buddy? I can't reason with them.

98
00:03:48,567 --> 00:03:52,167
Some people just don't let you
down, y'know? Time to move!

99
00:03:52,167 --> 00:03:54,567
It's always time to move, lately.

100
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:56,667
It might be a problem when I sleep.

101
00:03:56,667 --> 00:03:57,809
This looks big enough...

102
00:03:58,767 --> 00:04:00,433
Oh, we're going to make this work.

103
00:04:00,433 --> 00:04:02,167
No, this IS happening.

104
00:04:02,167 --> 00:04:03,000
Yeah.

105
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,067
Eh, it's just as well I'm not on foot.

106
00:04:05,067 --> 00:04:07,467
I'm not sure anybody would
pick me up as a hitchhiker;

107
00:04:07,467 --> 00:04:10,400
I'm dripping wet,
have cuts all over my face,

108
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:12,400
I might still be bleeding, I don't know.

109
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,333
Oh no...

110
00:04:13,333 --> 00:04:13,833
REBEL 1: Hey!

111
00:04:13,833 --> 00:04:14,833
Holy sh--!

112
00:04:14,833 --> 00:04:15,700
REBEL 1: You're Freeman, aren't you?

113
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:17,033
Jesus Christ!

114
00:04:17,033 --> 00:04:19,500
REBEL 2: I wouldn't believe it if
I couldn't see it with my own eyes!

115
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,233
REBEL 2: Doctor Gordon Freeman himself!

116
00:04:21,233 --> 00:04:22,167
Recognize!

117
00:04:22,167 --> 00:04:24,431
Yeah, no time for love, gotta go!

118
00:04:25,233 --> 00:04:25,800
Oof!

119
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,600
What is this, the Panama Canal?!

120
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:30,800
REBEL 1: ...before the Combine picks us
up. We're just getting ready to pull out.

121
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,600
Good! You can be my escort!

122
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:35,433
REBEL 2: We'd better hurry. We've got to
tear down this camp and get out of here.

123
00:04:35,433 --> 00:04:36,700
No! You need to go, NOW!

124
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:39,367
WUAH!
VORTIGAUNT: Greetings to the Freeman.

125
00:04:39,367 --> 00:04:40,900
What the fuck?!

126
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:42,733
REBEL 2: Come on in. I'll show
you what you're up against.

127
00:04:42,733 --> 00:04:44,533
Are you serious?!

128
00:04:44,533 --> 00:04:47,933
Oh, I guess he's your slave, but
you're letting him hold a gun!

129
00:04:47,933 --> 00:04:51,533
I'm sure it's not loaded but
that's WAY too much, guys!

130
00:04:51,533 --> 00:04:54,033
Well, looks like we found our mole!

131
00:04:54,033 --> 00:04:57,300
Hey, do you think there's any
chance we can stuff him in my suit,

132
00:04:57,300 --> 00:05:00,867
then send him out on the
boat? It would be win-win.

133
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:03,100
What can I say?  It's my physics background.

134
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:05,800
We're always looking to balance equations.

135
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:06,533
Oh, a map!

136
00:05:06,533 --> 00:05:07,667
REBEL 2: Here, take a look at this.

137
00:05:07,667 --> 00:05:08,600
Can I keep this?

138
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,367
REBEL 2: This here's the
dam. It's just up ahead.

139
00:05:10,367 --> 00:05:11,333
It's mounted...

140
00:05:11,333 --> 00:05:12,367
REBEL 2: Eli's hideout is here...

141
00:05:12,367 --> 00:05:14,000
What?
REBEL 2: ...a stone's throw from the apron

142
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,533
REBEL 2: and nestled in the old hydro plant.

143
00:05:15,533 --> 00:05:16,133
"Apron"?

144
00:05:16,133 --> 00:05:17,100
REBEL 2: But getting there,

145
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:19,800
REBEL 2 with that Hunter-Chopper
on your ass, next to impossible.

146
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:21,833
YEAH, TELL ME SOMETHING I DON'T KNOW!

147
00:05:21,833 --> 00:05:24,433
THIS HAS BEEN THE
WORST EXPERIENCE OF MY LIFE!

148
00:05:24,433 --> 00:05:27,233
REBEL 2: Good news is, the vortigaunt's
working his magic on your airboat...

149
00:05:27,233 --> 00:05:27,600
What?!

150
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,933
REBEL 2: ...so you'll have a little
more firepower going forward.

151
00:05:28,933 --> 00:05:30,100
You're touching my boat?!

152
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:30,867
REBEL 2: I think he's just finishing up now.

153
00:05:30,867 --> 00:05:31,667
Oh my God...

154
00:05:33,267 --> 00:05:35,367
GET THE FUCK BACK!

155
00:05:35,367 --> 00:05:37,367
I will SO kill you!

156
00:05:37,367 --> 00:05:38,533
This was a mistake!

157
00:05:39,667 --> 00:05:40,400
SHUT UP!

158
00:05:41,433 --> 00:05:44,133
There's a REASON I've stayed alive so long!

159
00:05:44,133 --> 00:05:47,967
IT'S BECAUSE I CAN SMELL PEOPLE
WHO ARE GOING TO GET ME KILLED!

160
00:05:47,967 --> 00:05:48,740
Open the gate!

161
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:50,167
OPEN THE FU--

162
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:51,767
You're welcome!

163
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:55,533
Damn, this veers to left now.

164
00:05:55,533 --> 00:05:58,367
I'm afraid to touch the gun; he
might have rigged it to blow.

165
00:05:58,733 --> 00:06:00,080
Can't steer...

166
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:01,300
[Hunter-chopper charging]
What?

167
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:03,467
[Hunter-Chopper firing]
AAAH! AHH!

168
00:06:03,467 --> 00:06:05,067
[Hunter-Chopper firing]
USE THE GUN!

169
00:06:05,067 --> 00:06:06,167
[Hunter-Chopper firing]
NO!

170
00:06:06,167 --> 00:06:08,600
NOOOO!

171
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:10,900
AAAAAAAH!

172
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:13,433
NO! THE GUN STOPPED! IS IT OVERHEATING?!

173
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:15,333
DIE!

174
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:17,100
YOU NEED TO DIE!

175
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:18,800
YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND!

176
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:20,267
NO! COME BACK!

177
00:06:20,267 --> 00:06:21,733
I HAVE TO HELP HIM!

178
00:06:21,733 --> 00:06:23,667
I HAVE TO HELP BOTH OF US!

179
00:06:23,667 --> 00:06:25,767
Oh my God!

180
00:06:25,767 --> 00:06:27,567
Well, I know MORE now!

181
00:06:27,567 --> 00:06:28,567
Oh wait. Here we go.

182
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:30,600
Jazz hands!

183
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,367
OOF!

184
00:06:31,367 --> 00:06:32,767
Whoa-ohhoohh!

185
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:35,267
Well the alien put a tracker on me for sure.

186
00:06:35,267 --> 00:06:37,467
The chopper wasn't watching the exit.

187
00:06:37,467 --> 00:06:40,433
He flew down low and opened
fire on me into the tunnel

188
00:06:40,433 --> 00:06:41,900
before I could even see him!

189
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:45,000
[alarm]
Oh boy! Okay! Who did that?

190
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:46,567
Who wants the Freeman?

191
00:06:46,567 --> 00:06:47,195
Anyone?

192
00:06:47,738 --> 00:06:48,372
Anyone?

193
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:49,933
Bueller?

194
00:06:49,933 --> 00:06:51,633
I'm not paid by commission.

195
00:06:51,633 --> 00:06:53,367
If this is a no-show, I'll leave.

196
00:06:53,367 --> 00:06:56,233
My services are in high demand elsewhere.

197
00:06:56,233 --> 00:06:57,533
Too high.

198
00:06:57,533 --> 00:06:58,067
[single gunshot]

199
00:06:58,067 --> 00:06:59,467
I heard that!

200
00:06:59,467 --> 00:07:02,463
This is a pretty crappy trap, actually.

201
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:04,700
Wait a minute. Whose side am I on?

202
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:05,533
What?

203
00:07:05,533 --> 00:07:08,700
Oh, now I get it! Now I get it!

204
00:07:08,700 --> 00:07:11,133
You were going to box me
in, pummel me with rockets,

205
00:07:11,133 --> 00:07:13,100
but then you realized you
couldn't see over the gate.

206
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:14,000
Whoa!

207
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:18,267
Will this damn gun ever
STOP OVERHEATING?! BLAH!

208
00:07:18,267 --> 00:07:21,367
I'M NOT PAYING YOUR STUPID
TOLL! SEND ME A TICKET!

209
00:07:21,367 --> 00:07:23,700
OH WAIT! I DON'T HAVE A LICENSE PLATE!

210
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:26,167
FUCK YOUUUUUUUUUU!

211
00:07:26,167 --> 00:07:28,800
FUCK YOU, TOOOOOOOOOO!

212
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:31,033
Yeah, let me through! I've got E-ZPass!

213
00:07:31,033 --> 00:07:33,233
Wow, this is almost relaxing.

214
00:07:33,233 --> 00:07:36,000
Only five or six bullets
instead of a thousand.

215
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,365
That chopper was a real source of stress.

216
00:07:38,967 --> 00:07:41,033
It's just a toxic relationship.

217
00:07:41,033 --> 00:07:43,467
But yeah, there's a tracker on me somewhere.

218
00:07:43,467 --> 00:07:45,333
They tipped their hand in that tunnel.

219
00:07:45,333 --> 00:07:47,717
But y'know what?
I shouldn't assume too much.

220
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:49,467
Whoa!

221
00:07:49,467 --> 00:07:50,933
It might not be in the gun.

222
00:07:50,933 --> 00:07:52,167
Oh, come ON!

223
00:07:52,167 --> 00:07:54,936
It's a nice evening and you're doing this?!

224
00:07:54,936 --> 00:07:56,967
AHHH-AHHHHHHH!

225
00:07:56,967 --> 00:07:59,033
WHY CAN'T YOU BE HAPPY FOR ME?!

226
00:07:59,033 --> 00:08:01,667
THAT WOULD'VE BEEN THE PERFECT
SPOT TO SHOOT FIREWORKS!

227
00:08:01,667 --> 00:08:05,600
I HATE GETTING SHOT AT FROM
ABOVE WITH AUTOMATIC WEAPONS!

228
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:07,600
NO! NOT YOU, TOO!

229
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:09,167
I'VE BEEN HURT ALREADY!

230
00:08:09,167 --> 00:08:11,167
CAN'T YOU SEE I'M VULNERABLE?!

231
00:08:11,167 --> 00:08:14,800
Wish I knew how much ammo was
in this gun. I forgot to ask.

232
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:17,567
Eh, it doesn't matter. They
would've lied to me anyway.

233
00:08:17,567 --> 00:08:20,367
They would--Oh shit! That's
him! That's the spook!

234
00:08:20,367 --> 00:08:22,333
[machinegun fire]
He's right there! I saw him!

235
00:08:22,333 --> 00:08:23,900
Will you stop shooting?

236
00:08:23,900 --> 00:08:25,567
God... I don't believe it.

237
00:08:25,567 --> 00:08:27,633
No, I DO believe it. I just--

238
00:08:27,633 --> 00:08:29,300
He WANTED me to see him.

239
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:31,767
He could've watched from
a window if he didn't.

240
00:08:31,767 --> 00:08:34,433
Hot damn, this is demoralizing!

241
00:08:34,433 --> 00:08:38,467
And he just happens to show up
with the helicopter's not around!

242
00:08:38,467 --> 00:08:39,633
Mm-hmm!

243
00:08:39,633 --> 00:08:41,967
But seriously. The tracker
could've been on me the whole time,

244
00:08:41,967 --> 00:08:43,800
and they only gave it away back there.

245
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:47,400
It could be on the boat,
my suit, my clothes...

246
00:08:48,033 --> 00:08:48,767
Fuck...

247
00:08:48,767 --> 00:08:50,067
When did it happen?

248
00:08:50,067 --> 00:08:51,467
Whooooaaaa...

249
00:08:51,467 --> 00:08:52,567
Oof.

250
00:08:52,567 --> 00:08:55,633
Yeah, things didn't get really
bad until I left the lab.

251
00:08:55,633 --> 00:08:58,400
I mean, they got bad at that
commune, but that was a raid.

252
00:08:58,400 --> 00:09:00,700
That felt more like wrong place, wrong time.

253
00:09:00,700 --> 00:09:04,733
More barrels. We're back to
Donkey Kong, huh, guys? Works for me.

254
00:09:04,733 --> 00:09:05,400
[machinegun fire]

255
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:06,667
[machinegun fire]
Oh no! Stop!

256
00:09:06,667 --> 00:09:07,433
[machinegun fire]
GO!

257
00:09:07,433 --> 00:09:09,233
JESUS CHRIST!

258
00:09:09,233 --> 00:09:12,400
WHO KNEW DRIVING A BOAT
ON LAND WAS A BAD IDEA?!

259
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:13,733
I CAN'T STEER!

260
00:09:14,633 --> 00:09:16,833
WAAAAAAAAAAAAAH!

261
00:09:16,833 --> 00:09:17,667
UHH!

262
00:09:17,667 --> 00:09:19,100
WILL YOU GET OFF MY BACK?!

263
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,100
I'D LIKE TO SEE *YOU* DRIVE THIS THING!

264
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:23,467
NOW GO SHOOT EACH OTHER IN THE CROSSFIRE!

265
00:09:23,467 --> 00:09:25,233
YOUR FRIEND IN THE VEHICLE DID!

266
00:09:25,233 --> 00:09:26,733
THAT'S HOW YOU DRIVE!

267
00:09:26,733 --> 00:09:28,133
In fact, now I'm doubting that--

268
00:09:28,133 --> 00:09:29,167
WHOA!

269
00:09:29,167 --> 00:09:31,133
--that those mortars were on purpose.

270
00:09:31,133 --> 00:09:33,800
The mortars stopped
once they hit that tower.

271
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:34,967
OOF!

272
00:09:34,967 --> 00:09:36,167
AHH!

273
00:09:36,167 --> 00:09:38,100
Gonna have some bruises...

274
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:42,367
Yeah, now I'm thinking them blowing up
their own buildings wasn't part of the plan.

275
00:09:42,367 --> 00:09:46,367
It could be that someone is in even
WORSE trouble than me right now.

276
00:09:46,367 --> 00:09:49,500
That sounds impossible
but I haven't been caught.

277
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:50,733
Ah, jinx.

278
00:09:50,733 --> 00:09:54,700
Actually, no! I'm pretty sure
these guys aren't here to CATCH me.

279
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:56,367
Or rather, they're here to catch--

280
00:09:56,367 --> 00:09:57,067
OOF!

281
00:09:57,067 --> 00:09:59,533
Shit, don't stop... Go go go go go go!

282
00:09:59,533 --> 00:10:01,633
HEY GUYS! I THINK YOU NEED MORE ROCKETS!

283
00:10:01,633 --> 00:10:04,333
NOBODY'S GOING TO TAKE YOU
SERIOUSLY WITH THIS FEW!

284
00:10:04,333 --> 00:10:07,833
Yeah, they're taking the dynamite
fishing approach to catching me!

285
00:10:07,833 --> 00:10:09,833
That probably is how they fish.

286
00:10:09,833 --> 00:10:13,467
Their brains probably don't even make
a distinction between me and a fish.

287
00:10:13,467 --> 00:10:16,700
I bet an MRI scan would
show no difference at all.

288
00:10:16,700 --> 00:10:18,633
C'mon! Eat it! EAT IT!

289
00:10:18,633 --> 00:10:20,467
OH! I BUSTED YOUR ENGINE!

290
00:10:20,467 --> 00:10:23,233
I appreciate how you guys
aren't leading your shots!

291
00:10:23,233 --> 00:10:25,700
You probably thought I
hadn't noticed, but I have!

292
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:27,933
Have you thought about what
I said about more rockets?!

293
00:10:27,933 --> 00:10:30,300
OH! BAD PLACE TO STOP!

294
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:32,633
YEAH, THAT'S AN ILLEGAL PARKING, FOR SURE!

295
00:10:32,633 --> 00:10:34,233
I'M WITH YOU ON THAT ONE!

296
00:10:34,233 --> 00:10:36,167
OKAY! TIME FOR ANOTHER LAP!

297
00:10:36,167 --> 00:10:38,700
I hope you guys have been
clocking me because I haven't.

298
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:40,367
Chugga-chugga-chugga-chugga-chugga-chugga--

299
00:10:40,367 --> 00:10:42,067
HO-HOO!

300
00:10:42,067 --> 00:10:42,700
Tire.

301
00:10:42,700 --> 00:10:45,833
Yeah, this is harder than NASCAR
because I also have to turn right

302
00:10:45,833 --> 00:10:47,433
when I try to kill other drivers.

303
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:50,600
HO-HOOOOO! GOLD CUP!

304
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:53,300
Time for champagne and to
gun down any survivors!

305
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:54,800
Alright!

306
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:55,933
None there...

307
00:10:55,933 --> 00:10:56,967
And a quick check...

308
00:10:59,133 --> 00:11:00,200
Looking good!

309
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,933
I'd like to thank my gun,

310
00:11:01,933 --> 00:11:04,067
and I would thank the
people who gave it to me,

311
00:11:04,067 --> 00:11:06,367
but they got me into
this mess to begin with,

312
00:11:06,367 --> 00:11:09,767
and those two things really
don't cancel each other out.

313
00:11:09,767 --> 00:11:14,000
I may have to eventually go back
and kill them. I don't know yet.

314
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,267
See, that--OOF!

315
00:11:15,267 --> 00:11:16,933
Excuse you!

316
00:11:16,933 --> 00:11:17,938
Okay...

317
00:11:19,067 --> 00:11:20,657
Yeah, I'm lost again.

318
00:11:23,833 --> 00:11:24,667
Hm.

319
00:11:24,667 --> 00:11:27,345
I guess the universe isn't
collapsing on itself.

320
00:11:28,267 --> 00:11:30,344
I'm not sure if I'm disappointed or not...

